  "question": {
    "text": "In the given circuit, what is the current ( in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>&nbsp;) through the battery?<br />\r<img src=\"assets\\qt0036_f4e53fa5669d.jpg\" style=\"width: 270px; height: 391px;\" />"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "In the given circuit diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> is reverse biased, so it will not conduct. Diode <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are forward biased, so they will conduct, Thus the equivalent circuit is<br /><br /><img src=\"assets\\st0036_728fd0bbeb33.jpg\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 365px;\" /><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>∴</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>net</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>16</mn></mrow><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Ω</mi></math><br /><br /><math><mo>∴</mo></math> current through the battery,<br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mi>net</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mfrac><mn>16</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math>"
  }
